.TH SOMBRAD 8 "2026-08-09" "sombra" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sombrad \- thermal, noise and backlight daemon for the ASUS Zenbook 14 UX3405MA
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sombrad
.RI [ --root " " path ]
.RI [ --config " " file ]
.RI [ --state " " file ]
.RI [ --ring " " file ]
.RI [ --bus-address " " address ]
.RI [ --capacity " " records ]
.RI [ --interval-ms " " ms ]
.RI [ --max-ticks " " n ]
.RI [ --no-dbus ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keeps the machine inside a chosen thermal envelope, follows the ambient light
sensor, and records one telemetry sample per second so that the envelopes can
be tuned from data rather than from guesswork.
.PP
It is the sole owner of the thermal controls. Two processes writing the same
sysfs nodes produce race-dependent behaviour rather than redundancy, which is
why the vendor daemon is masked rather than layered on top of, and why this one
refuses to start when another is already answering on its bus name.
.PP
Setpoints are static per mode. There is no feedback controller: measurement
showed static values handle both idle and sustained load. The emergency thermal
guard is not regulation but a safety interlock — it is active regardless of
mode, it only ever lowers, and it is the one thing that will drive the fan by
itself.
.PP
Normally run by systemd as
.BR sombrad.service .
The options exist so that a test run and a service run differ only in their
arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --root " path"
The root of the kernel control surface. Default
.IR / .
Pointing it at a directory of ordinary files is how the daemon is exercised
without hardware.
.TP
.BI --config " file"
The settings file. Default
.IR /var/lib/sombra/settings.conf .
Written by the daemon, and absent until the first change.
.TP
.BI --state " file"
What survives a reboot. Default
.IR /var/lib/sombra/state .
.TP
.BI --ring " file"
The telemetry ring. Default
.IR /var/lib/sombra/metrics.ring .
.TP
.BI --bus-address " address"
The bus to answer on. Empty, the default, means the system bus. An address points
the daemon at a bus of its own and exists for testing; from a build tree that is
the only thing that works, because claiming the name on the system bus needs the
policy file this package installs.
.TP
.BI --capacity " records"
Ring capacity in samples, overriding the retention in the settings file. Without
it the depth comes from
.B retention_days
there, seven days at 1 Hz by default. Retention is a property of the geometry:
the blocks are reserved once and the oldest record is overwritten in place, so
there is no growth and no cleanup task to fail.
.TP
.BI --interval-ms " ms"
The sampling interval. Default 1000.
.TP
.BI --max-ticks " n"
Stop after this many ticks. Zero runs until signalled.
.TP
.B --no-dbus
Do not claim the desktop power-profile names. Those are compatibility for the
panel applet; the daemon's own interface is claimed either way.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
Restore the hardware and exit. Automatic fan control is restored on every exit
path the daemon controls, and the unit's
.B ExecStopPost
covers the one it does not: a fan left behind by a dead daemon is a defect, and
nothing else will pick up after it.
.SH D-BUS
The daemon's own interface is
.B io.github.svesh87.Sombra
at
.IR /io/github/svesh87/Sombra ,
and it is the only way anything drives this daemon. Readings and settings are
properties, so a client reads them once with
.B GetAll
and is told what changes afterwards; what moves every tick travels as one
dictionary,
.BR Readings ,
and everything that changes when somebody changes it is a property of its own.
Every method is checked against the polkit action
.B io.github.svesh87.Sombra.manage
with interaction disabled, so a dialog never appears:
.B allow_active
answers it or nothing does. The definition of the interface is installed as
.IR /usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/io.github.svesh87.Sombra.xml .
.PP
Without a bus the daemon still runs. It owns the thermal envelope, so it keeps
managing the machine and claims the name once a bus appears.
.PP
For compatibility it also answers on
.BR net.hadess.PowerProfiles " and " org.freedesktop.UPower.PowerProfiles
— the standard interface, and the primary one — and on
.B com.system76.PowerDaemon
for the COSMIC panel applet. The vendor interface spells its profile names with
a capital letter and the standard one does not; the applet compares the answer
against a hard list and panics on anything else.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/sombra/settings.conf
.TP
.I /var/lib/sombra/state
.TP
.I /var/lib/sombra/metrics.ring
The telemetry. Its depth is
.B retention_days
in the settings file, and switching
.B enabled
off there stops the appending without touching the file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sombra/metrics.ring.bak
A ring this build cannot read, kept rather than deleted. One slot, replaced
whenever another such ring is found.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/io.github.svesh87.Sombra.conf
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.svesh87.Sombra.policy
Who may own the name, who may talk to it, and what polkit decides about a caller.
Without the first the daemon cannot claim its name; without the second every
command is refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sombra (1),
.BR sombra-tray (1)
